      "_id": "69e919427dea335c2b25772e",
      "latePostId": "69e73bad6013b43447173960",
      "content": "When ChatGPT confidently tells you something false, it doesn't know it's wrong. Here's the exact mechanism 🤖\n\nHow LLMs actually work:\n\nWhat people think:\n→ AI looks up information and reports it\n→ Like a very fast search engine with better language\n\nWhat's actually happening:\n→ LLM predicts the most statistically likely next token\n→ Based on: billions of parameters encoding patterns from training data\n→ No fact database being queried\n→ No internal 'true/false' check\n→ Just: 'what word sequence is most likely given this input?'\n\nWhy this causes hallucination:\n→ If training data was rich on a topic: high-quality output\n→ If training data was sparse, contradictory, or question is in a gap:\n→ Model generates a plausible-sounding sequence anyway\n→ It's confident. It's fluent. It's wrong.\n→ The model has no signal that it's confabulating\n\nThe structural nature of the problem:\n→ This is NOT a bug that can be patched\n→ It's a fundamental property of autoregressive language modeling\n→ Same mechanism that makes LLMs creative and fluent → also makes them hallucinate\n→ You cannot remove hallucination without removing the generative capability\n\nMost dangerous hallucinations:\n→ Plausible citations (real author, fabricated paper)\n→ Real-sounding statistics ('studies show 73%...')\n→ Names that almost exist (wrong middle name, wrong institution)\n→ Legal/medical advice that sounds authoritative\n\nWhat reduces (but doesn't eliminate) it:\n→ RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation): grounds responses in retrieved docs\n→ Grounding to external APIs/databases\n→ Constitutional AI and RLHF training\n→ None of these solve the underlying mechanism\n\nThe right mental model:\n→ Not a search engine\n→ Not a fact database\n→ A very well-read person who sometimes makes things up — confidently\n\n#aifacts #llm #hallucination #chatgpt #aiexplained #artificialintelligence #howaiworks #llmhallucination #aitruth #techeducation",
