      "_id": "69e8e9527dea335c2b24072c",
      "latePostId": "69e73ba66ded4b6ae06945f2",
      "content": "In 2021, an AI predicted the structure of every known protein on Earth — solving a 50-year-old biology problem in 18 months 🔬🤖\n\nThe Protein Folding Problem:\n\nWhat proteins are:\n→ Molecular machines running every process in every living organism\n→ Made of amino acid chains (sequence determined by DNA)\n→ Function determined by 3D folded shape — NOT sequence alone\n→ Wrong fold = no function (or harmful function)\n\nThe problem (1962-2020):\n→ Anfinsen's 1972 Nobel: sequence SHOULD determine structure\n→ But computationally predicting how it folds: ~50 years of failure\n→ Experimental methods: X-ray crystallography, cryo-EM\n→ Time per structure: weeks to months\n→ Cost per structure: $50,000-$500,000+\n\nAlphaFold2 (DeepMind, 2020):\n→ CASP14 competition (Critical Assessment of Protein Structure Prediction)\n→ AlphaFold2 scored ~90 GDT (accuracy comparable to experimental methods)\n→ Previous best: ~40 GDT\n→ John Moult (competition organizer): 'beyond my expectations'\n\nThe database (2022):\n→ DeepMind applied AlphaFold to entire known proteome\n→ 200+ million protein structures predicted\n→ Every organism with sequenced genome covered\n→ Released entirely free to researchers globally\n\nImpact:\n→ Drug discovery: decades-blocked targets suddenly accessible\n→ Tropical disease research: parasite proteins mapped (previously took years per protein)\n→ Cancer biology: mutant protein behaviors predictable\n→ Nobel Prize in Chemistry 2024: Hassabis + Jumper\n\nWhy this matters:\n→ 50 years of individual experimental results (200,000 structures)\n→ AlphaFold: 200,000,000 structures in 18 months\n→ 1,000x more structural biology knowledge, made free\n\n#aifacts #alphafold #deepmind #proteinfolding #nobelprize #artificialintelligence #drugdiscovery #biology #aibreakthrough #sciencefacts",
